        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging near you",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging Florida",
        "lede": "Virtual staging is a digital marketing technique for real estate: a designer adds furniture and décor to photos of empty or cleared rooms so potential buyers can visualize the space, with no furniture delivered to the property. Half of Florida's buyers shop from another state, so the pictures do the showing — Bella's designers stage Florida listings in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "Browse the lookbook",
        "alt_link": "/pages/lookbook",
        "city": "Florida",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging works in the Florida real estate market",
        "market_text": "<p>Florida is a remote-buyer market: northern relocations, snowbirds and international purchasers routinely shortlist — and sometimes buy — from photos alone. When the buyer can't attend the open house, the listing photos are the open house, and an empty white-tile room doesn't sell a Florida lifestyle to someone scrolling from New Jersey in February.</p><p>The stock skews vacant, too — investor condos, estate sales and new spec builds — so whole-home staging is routine here. Virtually staging an entire 8-photo listing costs about what one month of physically staging a single room would.</p><p>Florida's selling calendar is also inverted relative to most of the country. The buying season peaks when northern buyers are escaping winter, which means listings need to look their best in months when much of the US market is quiet. Photos that are ready on demand matter more in a market whose busiest weeks arrive in January.</p><p>97% of buyers use the internet in their home search (NAR), and in Florida the online listing is often the only showing a remote buyer gets. Many buyers decide which homes to visit based on listing photos alone, so staged images make the first impression that decides whether a buyer books a visit — which is why virtual staging works so well in a state with so many vacant, seasonal, investment and second-home properties. Staged photos also tend to perform better online and on social media, where buyers often see a listing first.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Florida home staging, done virtually for each buyer",
        "local_text": "<p>Our designers stage coastal-bright for Miami and Fort Lauderdale condos, airy transitional for Orlando and Tampa family homes, and elegant looks for Naples and Sarasota. Every image is MLS-ready in 24 to 48 hours, disclosed as virtually staged.</p><p>Outdoor space gets staged as living space here rather than as an afterthought — lanais, pool decks and screened porches are where Florida listings win the scroll, and they photograph empty worse than any interior room.</p><p>Our design team works online, so there's no site visit or delivery to schedule anywhere in the state: order, upload your original photos and a designer handles the style and layout. Volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+ — so whole-home sets and investor portfolios cost less per photo.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "Miami, Fort Lauderdale, Palm Beach, Naples, Sarasota, Tampa, St. Petersburg, Orlando, Jacksonville"
      }
    },
