    "faq": {
      "type": "bella-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My buyers are all out of state. Does staging really change anything?",
            "answer": "It matters more, not less. A buyer in Ohio building a shortlist from photos has nothing else to judge on — an empty tile-floor room gives them no sense of scale or lifestyle, and it gets scrolled past in favour of a listing that looks like a home."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which MLS do you export for?",
            "answer": "Whichever your board uses — Stellar in Tampa Bay, Miami REALTORS® in the southeast, and the others around the state. Files come back at standard MLS specs, so they upload without re-exporting wherever you list."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you stage a lanai or pool deck?",
            "answer": "Yes, and we'd encourage it. Outdoor living is a big part of what Florida buyers are shopping for, and an empty screened lanai is one of the least appealing photos in a listing set. Staged, it becomes one of the strongest."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "The condo is furnished, but badly. Options?",
            "answer": "Furniture removal is included, so we can clear the existing furniture digitally and stage the room fresh. That's a common request on estate sales and older snowbird condos where the furniture dates the listing."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does virtual staging cost?",
            "answer": "Bella virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} per photo in Florida and everywhere else we work, with volume discounts of 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+. Furniture removal, unlimited revisions for two weeks and full usage rights are included — no subscription and no minimum."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does home staging cost in Florida?",
            "answer": "Physical staging is priced by the stager, the size of the home and how long the furniture stays, so Florida quotes vary; as a general benchmark it runs about $2,000–5,000 a month. Virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, once, with no rental period to extend if the listing sits through the off-season."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I virtually stage my home for free?",
            "answer": "Free AI apps can drop furniture into a photo, but the scale and finishes are generated, not designed. For designer staging, new Bella clients can claim a $40 voucher on our sign-up page to try it. Eligibility subject to Bella's approval."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging worth it?",
            "answer": "For most vacant Florida listings, yes. Staging is meant to make a property more appealing and help it sell faster, but it can't guarantee multiple offers or stronger offers. What it can do is make the photos count: 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search (NAR), and an out-of-state buyer judges the home from the listing photos. Virtual staging furnishes them for a one-time cost per photo."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What photos do I need for virtual staging?",
            "answer": "High-resolution, well-lit photos of each room, shot wide from a corner — bright Florida daylight helps. Empty rooms are ideal, but furnished ones work too because furniture removal is included. The better the original photos, the more realistic the staged images."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging legal in Florida?",
            "answer": "Yes, as long as the photos don't mislead buyers. Add furniture and décor only, don't hide defects or change permanent features, disclose that the images are virtually staged, and consider including the original photos alongside them. Check your MLS rules for exact labeling; every Bella order includes disclosure guidance."
          }
        }
      },
